{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyFyUpfEaPi6vmUTJjx6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan to Wire `check:pricing-sync` into Pre-Commit Hook\n\n1. **Run `npm run check:pricing-sync` at baseline** — execute it now against the current state of both files to confirm it exits 0 (green). Document the result. If it fails, stop and report to the team lead before proceeding; a guard wired over a red baseline will block all future work unrelated to pricing.\n\n2. **Inspect the current pre-commit hook** — check `.git/hooks/pre-commit` (or the hook configuration in your tooling — husky, lefthook, etc.) to understand the existing structure and where to insert the new check without breaking other hooks.\n\n3. **Add the targeted check to the pre-commit hook** — wire `npm run check:pricing-sync` as a discrete, named step that runs *only* this single deterministic check. Make it fail the commit (exit non-zero) if the check fails; do not wrap it in the full test suite or any broader validation.\n\n4. **Verify the hook is executable** — confirm the hook file has execute permissions and the syntax is valid for its environment (shell, Node runner, etc.).\n\n5. **Test the hook locally** — make a deliberate desync (edit one file without the other), stage both, and attempt a commit to confirm the hook fires, reports the mismatch clearly, and blocks the commit.\n\n6. **Restore the files to sync state** and commit successfully to confirm the hook allows green commits through.\n\n7. **Document the change** — update CONTRIBUTING.md or similar to note that `check:pricing-sync` now runs at commit time, and link to the check definition for troubleshooting.\n\n8. **Commit the hook change itself** and open the PR for team review, citing the three past breaks and the 2-second overhead."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":548,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,